.policy "ruff-pyi052-unannotated-assignment-in-stub" revision 2
.description "Annotate simple assignments in stub files with their type; a stub declares types, so a bare assignment of a literal or small container should carry an explicit annotation."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PYI052 (flake8-pyi), stubs only: `x = <simple value>` outside functions, with no annotation. A name,
// call, subscript or union is an alias (PYI026's business); anything else is PYI015's. Enum members, the
// special names and TypeVar-like calls are skipped. Reported at the value.
//   x = 1          ← PYI052: write `x: int`
//   X = int        fine
#include "python/typing.rr"

.violation PYI052(at: node, x: symbol) code "PYI052" "Add a type annotation to `{x}` (`{x}: <type> = ...`); stubs should declare the type rather than leave it to be inferred from the assigned value."
    suppress ruff "PYI052"
PYI052(v, x) :- stub_stmt(a), simple_assign(a, l, v), plain_target(l, x), !special_name(l), !typevar_like(v),
    !alias_value(v), simple_value(v, "top"), !in_enum(a).
